NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY DATA, APIS, AND ASSETS — THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE COVERS THE
JAKSAFE SOURCE CODE ONLY.

The camera metadata catalog bundled under `backend/src/data/cctvCatalog.json`
and all spatial, atmospheric, traffic, routing, and visual streams fetched from
third-party providers at runtime remain the property of their respective owners
and are NOT licensed under MIT. They are integrated for research, academic, and
situational-awareness visualization under each provider's terms:

  - OpenStreetMap & OSRM (Open Source Routing Machine):
    Road network geometry, turn-by-turn steps, and Nominatim geocoding data are
    licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 by OpenStreetMap
    Contributors (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).

  - Open-Meteo Air Quality API:
    Atmospheric telemetry (PM2.5, PM10, US AQI, NO2, O3) is provided under
    Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) (https://open-meteo.com/).

  - Public CCTV Network (DKI Jakarta / Regional Stream Providers):
    Camera coordinates and public HLS/snapshot streams are owned by their
    respective municipal and public-service operators. JakSafe brokers streams
    strictly for real-time road safety & flood inspection without archiving
    personal video feeds.

  - TomTom Traffic API, Google Maps Platform (Photorealistic 3D Tiles & Places),
    Cesium ion, and Google Gemini API:
    Fetched at runtime using your own configured API credentials and governed
    by each provider's respective Terms of Service, quota limits, and commercial
    use restrictions.

In short: the MIT grant applies solely to the software codebase in this
repository and does not extend to third-party geospatial datasets, imagery,
or live sensor streams.
